[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'AI generated commercials are becoming more common, but they are not all made in the same way. Some are built through a slow, controlled process, [music] planning shots, keeping characters consistent, refining lighting, and testing transitions. Others are built for scale, creating many ads for'

[00:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'different products, audiences, and platforms with much less manual production. I think of these as two production [music] models, creative control production and scale-driven production. Creative control production'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is about taking the time to shape one commercial with intention. Scale-driven production is about creating more useful variations faster. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; Hi, I\'m Kira, and in this video, I\'m'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'partnering with Loom Flow AI to experiment with both approaches. I\'ll share the workflows I tried for each one and explore how they work &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; and when each approach makes sense. Let\'s start with creative control'

[00:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'production. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; For this workflow, I want to create a luggage commercial for the luggage and backpack brand Swissgear. I\'ve chosen this spinner suitcase, which comes in several color options. Before generating anything, I spent some time'

[01:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'planning the creative direction. I usually start by looking for inspiration. Whenever I come across a creative commercial or transition that I think I might use someday, I save [music] it. Then, when I\'m working on a new idea,'

[01:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I go back through that collection instead of starting from scratch. For this ad, I found this Instagram video that I\'d saved earlier. I loved how the outfit changed seamlessly with every 360 degree turn, and I thought'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that transition style would work perfectly for showcasing different suitcase variants. Then I built my own concept around it. Instead of simply changing the suitcase colors, I decided that each color would represent a'

[01:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'different travel personality. Transition stays the same, each turn reveals a new personality. To plan the visuals, I uploaded images of all the suitcase color options into Chat GPT. &gt;&gt; [music]'

[01:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Along with the character sheet of the model who would appear in every shot, which is me, by the way. Then I asked Chat GPT to develop the creative direction for each scene by suggesting the mood, outfit, and action that best matched each travel'

[02:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'personality. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; That gave me a complete creative blueprint before I generated a single frame. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; Once the concept was finalized, I provided Chat GPT with a screenshot from the reference video, asking it to match'

[02:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the clean white studio background, and generate a detailed image prompt for each personality concept. Now it\'s time to generate the images. I\'ll be using GPT-2 image, but not'

[02:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'inside Chat GPT. You can generate these images here as well, but for this project, I decided to use Loom Flow AI because I\'ll be generating images, videos, and UGC ads all in the same [music] workflow. It also gives me'

[02:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'access to GPT-2 image in 4K quality, which is a nice bonus. Having everything in one workspace makes the workflow much smoother instead [music] of constantly switching between different websites. If you\'d like to follow along, you\'ll find'

[03:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the link in the description. I\'ll also share a few more things I liked about it later in the [music] video. To generate each image, I uploaded the character sheet of the model. Then I uploaded the corresponding'

[03:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'suitcase color, &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; pasted the prompt, selected the image settings, and generated the result. I repeated the same process for all five travel personalities, &gt;&gt; [music]'

[03:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; and finally created one additional hero shot featuring all the suitcases together. With all the images ready, it\'s time to animate them. For the video generation, I\'m using the C Dance 2 model. In my experience, it\'s one of the best models for creating smooth, complex'

[03:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'transitions like this. Before generating the video, I needed a prompt that accurately described the transition from my reference. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; So, I uploaded the reference video to Gemini and asked it to analyze the 360° rotation transition and describe it in'

[03:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'detail. Gemini is really good at analyzing any video. Then I uploaded all of my generated images except the final hero shot, which I\'ll animate separately. Explain the sequence I wanted in simple English and'

[04:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'asked Gemini to combine everything into a single 15-second prompt for Sea Dance 2 using the same transition style. It generated this detailed prompt. Now back in Loom Flow, I clicked on'

[04:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'image to video [music] and selected the Sea Dance 2 model. I kept Omni reference mode enabled, then uploaded all of my generated images along with the inspiration video. Next, I pasted the prompt and tagged'

[04:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'each image wherever it was referenced by simply typing at and selecting the corresponding image. I also tagged the inspiration video at the beginning of the prompt where the transition style was described.'

[04:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'After choosing the rest of the generation settings, [music] I clicked create. And here\'s the first result. Not quite what I was expecting.'

[05:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This is actually a good example [music] of why iteration is such an important part of AI production. Instead of guessing what went wrong, I uploaded both my generated video and the reference video to Gemini,'

[05:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; asked it to compare them, identify the issues, and suggest improvements to the prompt. It gave me a refined prompt, so I brought it back into Loom Flow and generated the video again. And this is much better.'

[05:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This is exactly the kind of result I was aiming for. The only thing I\'m not happy with is the background music, but I\'ll worry about that later. Finding the right music is honestly one of the most time-consuming parts of editing for me. Now, [music]'

[05:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'let\'s animate the final hero shot. Cool. With the videos ready, it\'s time for editing. I made some simple cuts and arranged the clips together.'

[06:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Then I added the end text and the Swiss Gear logo to make it feel like a proper brand commercial. At this point, the only thing missing was the music. I wanted a track that starts subtly, then builds up as the first transition begins, with every'

[06:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'transition hitting on a strong beat. That\'s the kind of rhythm I had in mind. Music is still the weakest part of my workflow, and it\'s something I\'m actively trying to improve. My first stop was Epidemic Sound. I even tried'

[06:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'its AI studio, but I couldn\'t find a track that matched the energy I was looking for. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; So, I went back to Gemini. I asked it to analyze the final video and generate a matching soundtrack using its Lyria'

[06:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'music feature. To my surprise, the result was actually pretty good. &gt;&gt; [music]'

[07:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; All right, with that, my first commercial is ready. It took almost a full day of planning, generating, iterating, [music] editing, and experimenting. This approach works well'

[07:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for hero commercials, &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; product launches, fashion campaigns, and other visually driven brand films, where every creative decision matters. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; But, not every project needs that level of refinement, and that\'s where a more'

[07:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'scalable workflow comes in. So now, I wanted to try the other approach, &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; scale-driven production. These are the kinds of ads you often see on TikTok, Instagram Reels, and Meta. Short videos'

[07:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that quickly communicate a product, a problem, or a reason to try it. For this experiment, I chose a portable blender from Amazon. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; This time, instead of creating one polished commercial, I want to generate'

[07:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '10 different UGC ads as quickly as possible using C Dance 2 inside Loom Flow. Loom Flow AI actually has a dedicated marketing studio for this. It takes care of most of the setup, making it much'

[08:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'faster to create product ads. I\'ll show you how it works, but first, I need some ad concepts. For that, I went to ChatGPT and pasted the Amazon product link along with a prompt asking it to research the'

[08:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'product, [music] identify the top pain points it solves, and write 10 unique 15-second UGC ad scripts, &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; each with a different marketing angle. I also asked it to suggest the ideal'

[08:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'actor for every script. You can find this prompt along with the other prompts in the description. Within a few moments, ChatGPT had researched the product and generated 10 different ad concepts.'

[08:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
